From: David Bienvenu <davidbienvenu@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 08:10:19 -0700
Subject: Test StartDragging abort when mouse button is up

Ensure SystemDragEnded and DragSourceEndedAt are called when
StartDragging is aborted because the mouse button is not down. Also
avoid calling TransformPointToCoordSpaceForView in EndDrag when the
source RenderWidgetHost view is the root view, preventing NOTREACHED
crashes in unit tests and allowing RejectDragFromHiddenWebContents to be
re-enabled.

Tested locally w/ the relevant part of crrev.com/c/8410155 reverted and
the new test failed.

Bug: 522564418,564239696
Change-Id: I21202ca2967c281fddff8eea525c9b6cc31218d8
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8428359
Reviewed-by: Dave Tapuska <dtapuska@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: David Bienvenu <davidbienvenu@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1703440}

